# This repository's provenance validators hash files byte-for-byte (e.g. the K17d record binds the
# sha256 of every src/geosim file; checkpoint provenance hashes src/**/*.py). A Windows checkout
# with git's default core.autocrlf=true would rewrite LF to CRLF and make every such record read
# STALE, so line-ending conversion is disabled for the whole tree: working trees are byte-identical
# to the committed blobs on every platform. An explicit attribute takes precedence over autocrlf.
* -text

# Windows batch files additionally keep their CRLF bytes as committed: cmd.exe mis-parses some
# LF-only constructs, and the Windows package CI verifies CRLF inside the built zip (produced from
# the committed blobs via `git archive HEAD`). Covered by `* -text`; kept explicit as documentation.
windows/*.bat -text
